# .claudeignore — the "don't look here" list.
#
# Same idea as .gitignore, different job. .gitignore says what git must not
# SAVE. This says what a coding assistant should not READ or SEARCH, so a
# question about the product does not get answered out of a folder of test
# props.
#
# NOTE: Claude Code itself does not read this file — it reads the deny list in
# .claude/settings.json, which is kept in step with this one. This file is here
# for the other tools that follow the convention, and because it is the
# readable version: the settings file is the same list written as JSON.
#
# Nothing here is deleted or unavailable. It is skipped by default and can
# still be opened by name when somebody actually wants it.

# ---- Dependencies & build output ----
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.cache/
coverage/

# ---- Binary test fixtures ----
# 6.2 MB, 92 files, 70 of them PDFs. The automated suite reads exactly two
# small .docx files out of all of it; the rest are props from a manual QA
# session and can be rebuilt by the scripts in test-fixtures/generators/.
test-fixtures/
fixtures/

# ---- Fonts ----
# 500 KB of base64. One line in fonts.css is 122,588 characters long.
# The app SERVES this — it is ignored for reading, never for deleting.
fonts/
*.woff
*.woff2
*.ttf
*.otf

# ---- Sample contracts ----
# Also served by the app (server.js mounts /sample-contracts). Skipped for
# reading only.
sample-contracts/

# ---- Binary document formats ----
*.pdf
*.docx
*.doc
*.xlsx
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.gz

# ---- Images ----
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.ico
*.webp
*.svg

# ---- Generated test output ----
test/chromium/shots/
test/chromium/lang-coverage.json
test/chromium/theme-tokens-baseline.json

# ---- Server runtime data ----
server/data/
server/data-*/

# ---- Append-only history logs ----
# Roughly 900 KB between them — search these on purpose, not by accident.
BUGLOG.md
SUMMARY.md
TESTREPORT.md
CHECKLIST.md
SESSION-NOTES.md
LOOP_REPORT.md
INVENTORY.md
findings.json

# ---- Standalone report pages, not app code ----
ux-review.html
REVIEW-internal-review.html
REVIEW-internal-review-demo.html
HaTi-Kenya-Pricing-Research.html

# ---- Logs, temp, secrets ----
*.log
scratchpad/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
package-lock.json

# ---- DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED ----
# CLAUDE.md, README.md, PLAN.md, AUDIT.md, the DESIGN-* and WORKORDER-* files,
# and everything under js/, server/, index.html and test/*.test.js. Those are
# the working files. Hiding them would make the tool worse at its job without
# making anything faster that matters.
